WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.386
Learn documents the whole procedure,

2
00:00:02.386 --> 00:00:05.475
one page per step, and the
build follows it exactly.

3
00:00:05.475 --> 00:00:07.674
You set up an authoring environment,

4
00:00:07.674 --> 00:00:10.825
write a desired state
configuration and compile it.

5
00:00:10.825 --> 00:00:14.600
You package it, and test it with
the same agent the servers run.

6
00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:17.935
You publish the package to
storage, optionally sign it,

7
00:00:17.935 --> 00:00:21.938
and generate a policy definition
that records the package's hash.

8
00:00:21.938 --> 00:00:24.226
Then you publish the definition to Azure.

9
00:00:24.226 --> 00:00:27.738
That's eight steps and eight
commands, all on the slide.

10
00:00:27.738 --> 00:00:29.538
The build replaces none of them.

11
00:00:29.538 --> 00:00:31.270
What it adds goes between them.
